+```
+
+## Timeouts on the command line
+
+The `httpx` command-line client accepts a `--timeout FLOAT` option controlling
+the timeout used for network operations. The value must be a finite, strictly
+positive number of seconds. Zero, negative values, infinities, and NaN are
+rejected with an error before any network call is made. Fractional seconds are
+allowed; the default remains 5.0 seconds.
+
+```console
+$ httpx --timeout 0.5 https://example.com
 ```
